direnv.nix
==========

WARNING: AI vibe-coded software; review before use.

An opinionated, fast direnv replacement written in Zig, with deliberately
limited features: environment variables and `use nix` / `use flake`. Nix
environments are cached. It intentionally behaves differently from direnv
(see CAVEATS); do not expect drop-in compatibility.

PERF

  Env-only median, 300 runs on Linux x86_64, including process launch:

                       direnv 2.37.1    direnv.nix
    Project reentry         12.43 ms       0.21 ms
    Unchanged environment    1.43 ms       0.24 ms

  Recorded in bench-results.json; excludes Nix evaluation.

  Elvish, real flake project (Go + zig cc dev shell), time from hook start
  until the environment is active; median, fresh elvish per sample:

                                   direnv.nix   direnv 2.37.1 + nix-direnv 3.1.2
    First load, Nix eval cache       130 ms       383 ms
    First load, full Nix eval        590 ms       854 ms
    Cached load                      1.1 ms        43 ms

  First load runs `nix print-dev-env` in both; nix-direnv also spawns bash
  and runs `nix flake archive`. Cached load needs no shell process here;
  nix-direnv sources its cached rc through bash. direnv.nix does not add GC
  roots for flake inputs, so a first load after garbage collection may
  refetch them.

SETUP

    nix profile install github:aca/direnv.nix

  Or download a static binary from the rolling `nightly` prerelease
  (unversioned; rebuilt on every push to master):

    https://github.com/aca/direnv.nix/releases/tag/nightly
    direnv-{x86_64,aarch64}-{linux,macos}, with SHA256SUMS

  The installed binary is named `direnv`.

  Or use the existing NixOS module with this package:

    # in flake.nix
    inputs.direnv-nix.url = "github:aca/direnv.nix";

    # NixOS configuration:
    programs.direnv = {
      enable = true;
      package = inputs.direnv-nix.packages.${pkgs.stdenv.hostPlatform.system}.default;
      nix-direnv.enable = false;
      enableXonshIntegration = false;
    };

  Allow projects (Bash/Zsh; or use NixOS environment.variables):

    # automatically allow these directories and their descendants
    export DIRENV_NIX_ALLOW_DIRS="$HOME/src/git.internal:$HOME/src/github.com/aca"

    # alternatively, allow everything
    export DIRENV_NIX_ALLOW_ALL=1

  Or allow one project explicitly (from its directory or any subdirectory):

    direnv allow    # grant this project directory
    direnv deny     # revoke the grant

  Add ONE hook, unless NixOS already installs your Bash/Zsh/Fish hook:

    Bash:    eval "$(direnv hook bash)"
    Zsh:     eval "$(direnv hook zsh)"
    Fish:    direnv hook fish | source
    Elvish:  eval (direnv hook elvish | slurp)

  Example .envrc:

    use flake
    export MY_VAR=hello

CAVEATS

  - Not compatible with direnv by design. Supports [export] NAME=value, unset NAME,
    use nix [file], use flake [local-path#shell] [--impure], and watch_file path
    only.
  - No arbitrary shell commands or shellHook execution. Flakes must be local.
  - Nix's TERM and TZ (build-sandbox values) are ignored; PATH and
    XDG_DATA_DIRS are prepended to the shell's values instead of replacing them.
  - Imported Nix files need explicit watch_file entries to invalidate the cache.
  - The Nix cache key ignores shell variables except NIX_*, HOME and
    XDG_CONFIG_*; run `direnv reload` after other changes Nix depends on.
  - `use flake` is pure unless `--impure` is given; `use nix` is always impure.
    Impure evaluation skips Nix's eval cache (~120 ms -> ~580 ms per
    re-evaluation here), so keep it opt-in.
  - While a project is loaded, DIRENV_DIR holds its directory (for prompts).
  - Prompt-time export is silent, including Nix failures; `direnv reload`
    shows Nix's error output.
  - Loading is blocked by default. DIRENV_NIX_ALLOW_DIRS uses colon-separated
    absolute paths; DIRENV_NIX_ALLOW_ALL=1 overrides the list. Set in your shell.
  - `direnv allow` grants a directory, not a .envrc revision: edits stay allowed.
    Grants live in $XDG_DATA_HOME/direnv.nix/allow, so clearing the cache keeps
    them. `direnv deny` only revokes the grant, not the environment variables.
  - Supports Bash, Zsh, Fish and Elvish. NixOS installs Bash/Zsh/Fish hooks;
    add Elvish's hook manually. In Elvish, use set-env instead of export for
    the allow policy; in Fish, use set -gx.
  - `direnv export json` prints changes as one JSON object, null meaning unset
    (for editor integrations). There is no `direnv hook json`.
